# Cloudflare Pages edge redirects — real HTTP 301s.
#
# These used to live in astro.config.mjs, but Astro's static `redirects` can
# only emit a meta-refresh HTML page carrying <meta name="robots" content="noindex">.
# Google may act on the noindex before following the refresh and drop the URL
# instead of consolidating its ranking signals into the target. A 301 at the
# edge consolidates properly.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# NOTE: astro.config.mjs uses build.format: 'file', so pages exist as
# /path.html and are also served extensionless. Both forms are covered below.

